# SvelteKit 2 Routing and Load

Cursor: SvelteKit 2 routes are file-based under `src/routes/`. Each segment is a directory; the role is encoded in the filename prefix `+`. Target: `@sveltejs/kit ^2.60.1`.

The companion `sveltekit-anti-patterns` rule rejects the SvelteKit 1 shapes (entries #17, #18, #20, #21, #39).

## File roles

| File                | Role                                                                |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `+page.svelte`      | The page component                                                  |
| `+page.ts`          | Universal load (runs on server then client)                         |
| `+page.server.ts`   | Server-only load + form actions (cookies, private env, db access)   |
| `+layout.svelte`    | Layout wrapper that renders `{@render children?.()}`                |
| `+layout.ts`        | Universal layout load                                               |
| `+layout.server.ts` | Server-only layout load                                             |
| `+error.svelte`     | Error boundary                                                      |
| `+server.ts`        | Non-page HTTP endpoint (REST handler)                               |

## `+page.ts` (universal load)

Runs on the server during SSR, then on the client during client-side navigation. Cannot use `cookies`, `locals`, or `$env/static/private`.

```ts
// src/routes/posts/[slug]/+page.ts
import { error } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { PageLoad } from './$types'

export const load: PageLoad = async ({ params, fetch }) => {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/posts/${params.slug}`)
  if (!res.ok) error(res.status, 'Failed to load post')
  return { post: await res.json() as Post }
}
```

The `satisfies PageLoad` form is also valid:

```ts
export const load = (async ({ params, fetch }) => {
  // ...
}) satisfies PageLoad
```

## `+page.server.ts` (server-only load + actions)

```ts
// src/routes/dashboard/+page.server.ts
import { redirect } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { PageServerLoad, Actions } from './$types'

export const load: PageServerLoad = async ({ locals, cookies }) => {
  if (!locals.user) redirect(303, '/login')
  return { user: locals.user }
}

export const actions: Actions = {
  logout: async ({ cookies }) => {
    cookies.delete('session', { path: '/' })
    redirect(303, '/login')
  },
}
```

## `+page.svelte` consumes `data`

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import type { PageData } from './$types'
  let { data }: { data: PageData } = $props()
</script>
<h1>{data.post.title}</h1>
```

`PageData` is generated; it merges all parent layout `load` returns plus this page's `load` return.

## `+layout.svelte` and snippets

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import type { Snippet } from 'svelte'
  let { children }: { children?: Snippet } = $props()
</script>

<header>...</header>
<main>{@render children?.()}</main>
<footer>...</footer>
```

## `+server.ts` for non-page endpoints

Export one function per HTTP method. Source: https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/routing#server

```ts
// src/routes/api/posts/+server.ts
import { json, error } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { RequestHandler } from './$types'

export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ url, locals }) => {
  const page = Number(url.searchParams.get('page') ?? 1)
  const posts = await locals.db.posts.list({ page })
  return json({ posts })
}

export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, locals }) => {
  if (!locals.user) error(401, 'Unauthorized')
  const body = await request.json()
  const post = await locals.db.posts.create(body)
  return json({ post }, { status: 201 })
}
```

## `depends()` for manual invalidation keys

```ts
import type { PageLoad } from './$types'
import { invalidate } from '$app/navigation'

export const load: PageLoad = async ({ depends, fetch }) => {
  depends('app:posts')
  return { posts: await fetch('/api/posts').then(r => r.json()) }
}

// Elsewhere, after a mutation:
await invalidate('app:posts')
```

## `parent()` for reading parent layout data inside child load

```ts
export const load: PageLoad = async ({ parent }) => {
  const { user } = await parent()
  return { user }
}
```

Avoid awaiting `parent()` if you do not need it; it serialises the load tree.

## `fetch()` that proxies cookies + reuses SSR responses

The `fetch` provided to `load` knows about same-origin endpoints, forwards cookies during SSR, and avoids a second network round-trip on the client by reusing the SSR response payload.

```ts
export const load: PageLoad = async ({ fetch }) => {
  // Same-origin: hits the SvelteKit handler in-process during SSR.
  const r = await fetch('/api/posts')
  return { posts: await r.json() }
}
```

## Route param patterns

| Pattern                    | URL examples                          | `params` shape                   |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `[slug]`                   | `/posts/hello`                        | `{ slug: 'hello' }`              |
| `[...rest]`                | `/files/a/b/c.txt`                    | `{ rest: 'a/b/c.txt' }`          |
| `[[optional]]`             | `/about` and `/about/team`            | `{ optional: undefined \| 'team' }` |
| `[id=integer]` (matcher)   | `/posts/42` only when `42` matches    | `{ id: '42' }` (always string)   |

Matcher example (`src/params/integer.ts`):

```ts
import type { ParamMatcher } from '@sveltejs/kit'
export const match: ParamMatcher = (param) => /^\d+$/.test(param)
```

## Route groups via `(group)` parens

Directories wrapped in parens are group folders that share a layout but do not appear in the URL.

```
src/routes/
  (marketing)/
    +layout.svelte
    +page.svelte         # /
    pricing/+page.svelte # /pricing
  (app)/
    +layout.server.ts    # auth gate
    +layout.svelte
    dashboard/+page.svelte  # /dashboard
```

## Why these matter for LLM output

Pre-2024 trained models will produce:

- `throw error(...)` / `throw redirect(...)` (anti-pattern #17)
- Top-level unawaited promises in `load` (anti-pattern #20)
- `goto('https://external')` (anti-pattern #21)
- `+page.ts` exports without `PageLoad` type (anti-pattern #39)
